*Rotary District 5040, November 20, 2018. Photos by Drew Antrobus.*

The newly renovated medical centre in the fishing village of Panglao, on the island of Panglao, Bohol, the Philippines, will receive used medical equipment such as hospital beds, side tables, medicine carts, wheelchairs, emergency beds and cribs for children in a shipping container organized and loaded on November 17, 2018, by Rotary members of Districts 5040 and 5050 in the Greater Vancouver area.

Also in the container, sponsored by Rotary World Help (supported by many Rotary clubs in the region and, in this case, by the Rotary Club of Coquitlam Sunrise), are dental chairs, dental equipment and supplies, plus computers and books. The Rotary Club of Panglao will administer distribution of the equipment and supplies when the container arrives in the coming weeks.

The dental equipment and supplies are being shipped ahead of a dental mission to Manila and Panglao to provide free dental care, such as cleaning, fillings and extractions, and to educate the young local graduate dentists who will volunteer during the mission. A group of dentists from the Vancouver Caring Hearts Dentistry Society and participants in the Rotary District 5040 Friendship Exchange are taking part in the February 2019 dental mission to Panglao and Manila. The Friendship Exchange group will distribute hygiene kits and provide food to children in need in Panglao.

The container also holds computers and books for a Rotary computer centre and library at a school in Panglao. Equipment and supplies for this shipment came from BC hospitals, UBC and Douglas College.

Since it was founded in 1992, the Rotary World Help Network has collected medical equipment and supplies, dental, optical, education and sports equipment, and disaster relief supplies valued at more than $136 million, and distributed them in 390 shipping containers to international recipients in need in 60 countries, benefiting an estimated 11.7 million people.
